---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { site } from '../../content';
const path = "/use-cases/reviews-and-ugc";
const title = "Shopify email apps for reviews and ugc: workflow guide";
const desc = "Collect honest feedback and reuse customer content with context.";
const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "When should requests send?",
    "answer": "After an opportunity to experience the item, using reliable delivery or access information and product-specific judgment rather than a universal day count."
  },
  {
    "question": "Can negative feedback remain eligible?",
    "answer": "Yes. Keep honest feedback invitations open and handle service issues separately from review selection."
  },
  {
    "question": "Which app should I choose?",
    "answer": "Choose after demonstrating collection, submission exits, product matching and permission handling in your actual stack; no supplier is universally best."
  }
];
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="container py-16 md:py-24">
    <a class="link" href="/use-cases">← All use cases</a>
    <p class="editorial-kicker mt-6">Reviews and UGC</p>
    <h1 class="hero-title mt-5 max-w-5xl">Shopify email apps for reviews and ugc: workflow guide</h1>
    <p class="mt-7 max-w-3xl text-xl leading-9 text-[#4a2d17]">Collect honest feedback and reuse customer content with context.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="container pb-12">
    <div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Separate collection from reuse</h2>
      <p>A request asks someone about a product they experienced. A marketing block presents selected feedback to another shopper. Give each job an owner, a source record and a success measure; collecting a photo does not establish permission for every later use.</p>
      <p>Inventory existing review requests before adding another sender. Choose one owner per order line and record request status, submission status, product ID and the content source so reminders can stop after submission.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="container pb-12">
    <div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Anchor requests to product experience</h2>
      <p>Use delivery information where reliable, then allow time appropriate to what the customer can assess. Fit can be assessed sooner than durability. If delivery events are missing, use a conservative estimate with an explicit uncertainty label rather than saying the parcel arrived.</p>
      <p>Partial shipments need line-level timing. Digital access is different from actual usage. Do not delay all critical feedback until the return window ends; a customer returning an item can still describe a useful experience.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="container pb-12">
    <div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Make the request answerable</h2>
      <p>Name the purchased item and ask a neutral question about fit, setup or use. Link directly to the correct review form. For a mixed basket, prioritize a manageable request rather than sending one message for every line.</p>
      <p>Offer a photo prompt when it helps explain the product, without making a photo mandatory. A gift purchaser may not be the user: offer a way to share the request rather than treating a recipient address as marketing permission.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="container pb-12">
    <div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Keep support and feedback open</h2>
      <p>Route complaints to a named support queue with response ownership. A service pause on unrelated promotional messages can be helpful, but it should not remove the person’s ability to leave an honest review or revoke earned benefits.</p>
      <p>Use the same invitation criteria regardless of expected sentiment. Do not send only happy survey respondents to the public review form. Any incentive proposal needs a check against current applicable rules and platform terms before launch; points are not an automatic exception.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="container pb-12">
    <div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Maintain a reusable content register</h2>
      <p>For each quote, photo or video, retain source URL, author reference, product, original wording, allowed channels, permission record and withdrawal status. Ask for clarification where the permission scope is unclear.</p>
      <p>Record cropping and edits and keep the original. Avoid edits that change the meaning. A public social post or review submission alone should not be treated as a blanket permission record for an advertising library.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="container pb-12">
    <div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Match proof to the decision</h2>
      <p>In browse or cart messages, select feedback relevant to the actual product or explain that it concerns a different item. Welcome messages can use a clearly labeled brand-level story; launch copy should not imply reviews exist for an unreleased product.</p>
      <p>When a SKU lacks relevant content, show education or omit the module. No fixed star average or review count guarantees usefulness. Include enough context for a reader to understand what the selected quote does and does not establish.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="container pb-12">
    <div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Handle changing ratings and withdrawn assets</h2>
      <p>Record the rating source, scope, count and retrieval date if using an aggregate. A saved email cannot update after delivery, so avoid presenting a stale snapshot as a live number. Check the landing page before sending.</p>
      <p>For dynamic blocks, define a fallback for empty responses, mismatched variants and unavailable images. Withdrawal should stop future use in scheduled campaigns and reusable templates; keep an audit of where the asset was used.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="container pb-12">
    <div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Compare collection and reuse separately</h2>
      <p>Measure submitted reviews against delivered eligible requests, with the same observation window across product cohorts. Track completion failures, duplicate asks and support response time as operational measures.</p>
      <p>To evaluate reuse, propose a randomized comparison of a relevant proof module and an otherwise equivalent message. Purchases and contribution matter alongside clicks. A higher click rate alone is not proof of incremental orders or a reason to book forecast lifetime value.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="container pb-12">
    <div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Choose the stack by a demonstration</h2>
      <p>Ask the current review tool and email provider to demonstrate line-level request deduplication, a submission exit, a product-matched module and a withdrawn-photo fallback. Confirm the exact integration and plan with current primary documentation before purchase.</p>
      <p>Compare keeping the current review collector with adding a curated manual module, an integration, or a consolidated stack. Include review volume, email sends, permissions administration, moderation and operator time in the cost model.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="container pb-12">
    <div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Release with a small content library</h2>
      <p>Proposed rehearsal: use staff records for split delivery, a submitted review arriving before a reminder, a gift order, a removed image and an empty product response. These are checks to perform, not reported test outcomes.</p>
      <p>Start with one product group and one placement. Keep the old request sender disabled before its replacement starts, preserve submission history and review both collection quality and content permissions before expanding.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="container pb-12"><a class="link" href="/use-cases/segmentation">Audience definitions →</a> · <a class="link" href="/use-cases/post-purchase">Post-purchase →</a> · <a class="link" href="/use-cases/product-launch">Product launch →</a></section>
  <FaqSection faqs={faqs} title="Reviews and UGC FAQ" />
</BaseLayout>
